@prefix gmeow:   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix logic:   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:     <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "GMEOW Logic"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The GMEOW Logic module — home of the `logic:` reasoning vocabulary. A minimal stub: the normative design is in `design/`, and the `logic:` terms, rules, profiles, and generators are minted when the engine lands (Principle 17). No terms are declared here yet, so the module adds no axioms to the reasoned core."@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:comment "Stub module. The logic: namespace <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> is reserved here; its vocabulary (the unified core, semantic profiles, the foundation UFO⁺, world/modal terms) is specified in design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md and minted with implementation. Until then this slice contributes only its identity and tier (the manifest), not ontology terms."@x-gmeow-english ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow> .

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# No terms yet. The `logic:` vocabulary (logic:Kind, logic:Relator,
# logic:rigidlyAppliesTo, logic:World, logic:counterfactualOf, the semantic
# and decidability profiles, …) is specified in design/ and minted when the
# native solver lands, together with its generators and conformance corpus
# (Principle 17, amendment-in-the-open).
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
